                <pb facs="0039" n="5" sameAs="frus:frus1955-57v06/pg5"/>

                <head>3. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>In connection with preparation of the second progress report on NSC 5432/1, <ref target="#d3"><hi
                            rendition="#italic">infra</hi></ref>, the Working Group on Latin America
                    prepared and concurred in a paper entitled “Detailed Development of Major
                    Actions Relating to NSC 5432/1, United States
                    Objectives and Courses of Action With Respect to Latin America,” covering
                    December 1, 1954–July 14, 1955. This paper, dated July 20, was a compilation of
                    reports received by the Working Group from the Departments of Defense, State,
                    and the Treasury, the International Cooperation Administration, and the United
                    States Information Agency, all of which were represented on the Working Group.
                    No formal action on the paper was taken by the Board Assistants or the
                    Operations Coordinating Board. The paper was distributed on an informal basis to
                        OCB member agencies, the National Security
                    Council staff, and other agencies, for background purposes and to <pb
                        facs="0040" n="6" xml:id="pg6"/> provide assistance in the briefing of
                    principals who acted on the progress report. (Department of State, OCB Files: Lot 62 D 430, Latin America—1955)</p>
            </div>
